A||||3||ChadMan||Summer's here - cooling ideas?||||1||
Z||000000||ChadMan||05-09-2000||09:20 AM||||If you're like me, you take your Fiero to lots of outdoor events - picnics, auto races, car shows, etc.<P>Has anyone found a decent-sized cooler that will fit in the Fiero's trunk?  I find myself paying $3 for Coke, $4 for beer and $6 for burgers because all I can get in my trunk is a little Playmate that barely holds a 6-pack.<P>I did find some great camper's chairs at Galyan's - they have backs and armrests but they're still small enough to fold and fit perfectly behind the Fiero's seats!  They're made by a French company called Lafuma if anyone cares.||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||05-09-2000||10:32 AM||||i was at wally world or sams, cant remember which one, but i saw a decent sized "crushable" cooler.  it would be perfect for the fiero.  it was in the camping section.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||05-09-2000||10:41 AM||||Chad:  It seems to me there are styrofoam coolers available that will wedge into the deep opening (as long as there's something underneath for them to rest on).  In fact, I think you can get two in there (side by side) if you're careful.  They're not much bigger than the Playmates but anything helps (I guess).<P>You're planning for Indy, aren't you!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||05-09-2000||12:34 PM||||I'm planning for Indy, Mid-Ohio, the Fiero Festival in Louisville, Mid-Ohio again in August...||||reg||10
